{"id":"0275c584-0ebe-4167-8fce-522be8730fa0","type":"level","createdDate":"2026-06-13T23:04:39.285Z","createdBy":"chaitanya.ponnapati@codeninjas.com","lastModifiedDate":"2026-06-13T23:04:39.285Z","lastModifiedBy":"chaitanya.ponnapati@codeninjas.com","attributes":{"tags":["CREATE"],"title":"Level 5","sequence":5,"activity":{"id":"0f2a4b88-3be6-4340-a5d6-2af36c79c32d","type":"activity","sequence":4,"group":{"id":"0f2a4b88-3be6-4340-a5d6-2af36c79c32d","type":"build","name":null,"sequence":11,"subgroups":[{"id":"0f2a4b88-3be6-4340-a5d6-2af36c79c32d","type":"subgroup","sequence":1,"name":"build 1","steps":[{"id":"b6da701e-cf50-4d4b-b97c-00f18ecc0d53","hints":"<p>❓Did you use the circle tool <img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/pw14jwaj.ibx.png\"> to draw a circle outline in black, positioned in the upper middle part of the canvas, then add the balloon knot and string, like this? </p><p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/ykzzgsw3.fty.png\"></p>","senseiHelp":"<p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/ann1nbkl.nts.png\"></p><p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/vntvfqnu.ibl.png\"></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Ask the ninja</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">:</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">❓ Why might the balloon image be created on a 32x32 canvas?</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">❓ How might pixels be arranged to draw the balloon knot and string?&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Sensei Pro Tip</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">:</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">💡 Point out to the ninja that the circle tool in the paint editor creates a circle from its center. That means that the ninja should position their mouse from wherever they want the center of the circle to appear.</span></p>","instructions":"<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Begin the project by drawing a balloon image!</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Click the </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Assets</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> menu along the top of the screen. Create a new image asset named </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">balloon0</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">. Change the canvas size to 32x32.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Use the circle tool to draw a circle outlined in black. Position the circle in the upper middle of the canvas.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Use the paint tool to draw the balloon knot and the string, like this:</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"></span><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/ljygcqa2.u0n.png\"></p>","text":null,"type":null,"image":null,"videoUrl":null,"mediaType":null,"questions":null,"badges":null,"reflectionQuestions":null},{"id":"2ee1e3e2-7545-4615-863f-b47abca1ed7a","hints":"<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">❓Did you duplicate the balloon asset, then fill it with a light color? </span></p><p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/wc3riv41.djj.png\"></p>","senseiHelp":"<p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/iffwuafl.c22.png\"></p><p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/b5apvb04.efw.png\"></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Ask the ninja</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">:</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">❓ What color might be used as the circle’s base color?</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Sensei Pro Tip</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">:</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">💡 If the ninja’s balloon string is drawn in black, encourage them to test out other colors for the string, too.</span></p>","instructions":"<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Add a base color to the balloon image!</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Duplicate the </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">balloon0 </strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">asset, then rename the new asset </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">balloon1</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Use the fill tool to add a base color inside the outline. Consider using a light color for the balloon, such as green (7).</span></p>","text":null,"type":null,"image":null,"videoUrl":null,"mediaType":null,"questions":null,"badges":null,"reflectionQuestions":null},{"id":"3a716d07-9c5a-4d77-a8d8-78dbcbd9d806","hints":"<p>❓Did you use <em>dithering </em>to add pixels in a <em>diagonal </em>pattern on the bottom right corner of the balloon image?</p><p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/hda0bmqr.2lb.png\"></p>","senseiHelp":"<p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/zxdd2iab.zq2.png\"></p><p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/znhmvhqj.wcj.png\"></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Ask the ninja</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">:</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">❓ What is </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">dithering</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">? Why is it used in pixel art?</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">❓ How might pixels be placed to draw a </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">form shadow</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> in the balloon image?</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Sensei Pro Tip</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">:</span></p><p><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">💡 Dithering</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> is a pixel art technique that creates texture by using patterns of pixels in a </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">diagonal </em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">or checkered pattern to ease the transition between 2 colors. Because there is typically a small palette of colors available when working in pixel art, it’s important to use pixel space and color wisely.</span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> </em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">By placing pixels strategically, the image can give the effect of having more dimensions than it would if there were no transition between the colors.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">💡 Encourage the ninja to tinker with the placement of the pixels to create a </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">form shadow </em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">in the bottom right corner of the balloon image. Remind the ninja that they can zoom in and out to see how the image appears at a smaller scale.</span></p>","instructions":"<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Use </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">dithering </em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">to add depth and </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">shadows</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> to the balloon image.</span></p><p><br></p><p><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Dithering </em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">is a pixel art technique that creates texture by using patterns of pixels in a </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">diagonal </em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">or checkered pattern to ease the transition between 2 colors.&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Duplicate the </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">balloon1 </strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">asset, then rename the new asset </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">balloon2</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Use the paint tool and an </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">analogous </em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">color, such as teal (6), to draw a </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">form shadow</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> on the bottom right corner of the balloon. Use </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">dithering</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> by drawing individual pixels in a spaced out </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">diagonal </em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">pattern. This will create a transition between the balloon and the </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">shadow</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">, and add depth</span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> </em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">to the image.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"></span><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/uobnxs5l.pg2.png\"></p>","text":null,"type":null,"image":null,"videoUrl":null,"mediaType":null,"questions":null,"badges":null,"reflectionQuestions":null},{"id":"bd963742-29b2-4e9b-8a4e-d6adc2919093","hints":"<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">❓Did you use </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">dithering </em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">to add pixels in a </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">diagonal </em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">pattern on the top left corner of the balloon image?</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"></span><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/ewhel0bw.2e0.png\"></p>","senseiHelp":"<p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/z00jiprz.yvr.png\"></p><p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/x2i2g3bj.lzf.png\"></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Ask the ninja</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">:</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">❓ How might pixels be placed to draw a </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">highlight </em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;in the balloon image?</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">❓ What color might be used to a add a </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">highlight</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> to the balloon image?</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Sensei Pro Tip</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">:</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">💡 </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Dithering </em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">is a pixel art technique that creates texture by using patterns of pixels in a </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">diagonal </em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">or checkered pattern to ease the transition between 2 colors. Because there is typically a small palette of colors available when working in pixel art, it’s important to use pixel space and color wisely.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">💡 Point out to the ninja that a very bright color should be used to draw the </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">highlight</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">.</span></p>","instructions":"<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Use </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">dithering </em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">to add </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">highlights </em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">to the balloon image.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Duplicate the </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">balloon2 </strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">asset, then rename the new asset </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">balloon3</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Use the paint tool to draw </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">highlights </em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">on the top left corner of the balloon in a very bright color, such as white (1).&nbsp; Use </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">dithering</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> by drawing individual pixels in a spaced out </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">diagonal </em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">pattern.</span></p>","text":null,"type":null,"image":null,"videoUrl":null,"mediaType":null,"questions":null,"badges":null,"reflectionQuestions":null},{"id":"beb19919-21e2-46c3-a0e1-6847c0556525","hints":"<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">❓Did you update the outline of the balloon to match the surrounding pixels’ colors?</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"></span><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/4yjl0xsv.oej.png\"></p>","senseiHelp":"<p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/m0vvwq2a.scd.png\"></p><p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/sdaxfwcw.yf3.png\"></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Ask the ninja</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">:</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">❓What colors should the black outline of the balloon image be replaced with?&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">❓Do you prefer the balloon image with the black outline or with no outline? Why might you use one over the other?</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Sensei Pro Tip</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">:</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">💡 Make sure the ninja has filled in the outline with the color that is directly next to it in the balloon image, so that there appears to be no outline.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">💡 Outlines can be used in different ways in pixel art. If a ninja wants an image to really stand out on screen, they may opt to keep a black outline to create a strong contrast between the image and the background. Alternatively, removing the outline (or blending it with the existing colors of the image) can create a smoother transition between the image and the background.</span></p>","instructions":"<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Replace the balloon’s black outline.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Duplicate the </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">balloon3 </strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">asset, then rename the new asset </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">balloon4</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">.&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Use the paint or fill tools to replace the outline of the balloon using the original base color and the </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">shadow</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> color. Match the colors of the outlines to the surrounding pixels’ colors.</span></p>","text":null,"type":null,"image":null,"videoUrl":null,"mediaType":null,"questions":null,"badges":null,"reflectionQuestions":null},{"id":"80daed7b-9f80-44a8-a628-7bffa27d955a","hints":"<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">❓Did you type </span><strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\" style=\"background-color: rgb(204, 204, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">assets</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">, a dot operator, the asset type and the asset name</span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> </strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">inside 2 backticks </span><span style=\"background-color: rgb(204, 204, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">``</span><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> for each element in the </span><strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\" style=\"background-color: rgb(204, 204, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">balloonArray</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">?</span></p>","senseiHelp":"<p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/ibwrubcg.um1.png\"></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Ask the ninja</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">:</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">❓Did you place the balloon image assets in the correct order in the </span><strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\" style=\"background-color: rgb(204, 204, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">balloonArray</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">?</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">❓ What background color might be used to display the balloon images on screen?</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Sensei Pro Tip</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">:</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">💡 Make sure the number of each image asset matches the corresponding index in the array so that each image adds onto the previous one.</span></p>","instructions":"<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Set the scene to display the balloon images on screen!</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Return to the JavaScript editor, then add a </span><strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\" style=\"background-color: rgb(204, 204, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">// project initialization</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> comment at the top. Below, declare a </span><strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\" style=\"background-color: rgb(204, 204, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">balloonArray</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> that stores the 5 balloon image assets.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Then, add a </span><strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\" style=\"background-color: rgb(204, 204, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">// project start</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> comment and set a background color underneath.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Click ▶</span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><em> </em></strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">to see the chosen background color appear on screen.</span></p>","text":null,"type":null,"image":null,"videoUrl":null,"mediaType":null,"questions":null,"badges":null,"reflectionQuestions":null},{"id":"7e6b87f1-b7c8-4afd-b325-7697e6139b24","hints":"<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">❓Did you add an xOffset value (</span><strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\" style=\"background-color: rgb(204, 204, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">25</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">) with a spacing value (</span><strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\" style=\"background-color: rgb(204, 204, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">25</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">), multiplied by the counter variable </span><strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\" style=\"background-color: rgb(204, 204, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">i</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> like this: </span><strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\" style=\"background-color: rgb(204, 204, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">(25 + (25 * i))</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">, to set each sprite’s x-position?</span></p>","senseiHelp":"<p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/5x0yvjcd.iyf.png\"></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Ask the ninja</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">:</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">❓ What values might you use to offset the sprites from the left side of the screen and to space out each sprite?</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">❓ How do the balloon images appear on screen?</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Sensei Pro Tip</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">:</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">💡 Encourage the ninja to test out their code to make sure the sprites are placed correctly on screen. Prompt them to consider which values should be added together and which should be multiplied to correctly position the images.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">💡 Point out to the ninja that they made small updates to the balloon image in each iteration. Have them compare the first and last images to see how the drawing progressed over time.</span></p>","instructions":"<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Display the balloon image from each step of the drawing process on screen!</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Under </span><strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\" style=\"background-color: rgb(204, 204, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">// project start</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">, use a </span><strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\" style=\"background-color: rgb(204, 204, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">for</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> loop to create 5 sprites. Use the loop’s counter variable to select a different image from the </span><strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\" style=\"background-color: rgb(204, 204, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">balloonArray</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">, each time the loop runs.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Set the x-position of the sprites by adding a value to offset the left side of the screen with the spacing between each sprite, multiplied by the loop’s counter variable. Set the y-position to a coordinate in the middle of the screen.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Click ▶</span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><em> </em></strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">to see each balloon image displayed on screen!</span></p>","text":null,"type":null,"image":null,"videoUrl":null,"mediaType":null,"questions":null,"badges":null,"reflectionQuestions":null},{"id":"c0649165-d992-4a0f-b378-5c3d4cc669c5","hints":"<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">❓Did you update all 4 parameters in the </span><strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\" style=\"background-color: rgb(204, 204, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">runImageAnimation</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> function so that the images in the </span><strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\" style=\"background-color: rgb(204, 204, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">balloonArray</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> continuously loop ?</span></p>","senseiHelp":"<p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/5smrili2.b1i.png\"></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Ask the ninja</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">:</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">❓ Why might the </span><strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\" style=\"background-color: rgb(204, 204, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">runImageAnimation</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> function be useful for showing multiple iterations of an image?</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">❓ What might the frameInterval and loop parameters be set to so that the images continuously rotate at a reasonable rate?</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Sensei Pro Tip</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">:</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">💡 The </span><strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\" style=\"background-color: rgb(204, 204, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">runImageAnimation</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> function can be useful for showing how an image changes over time. In this context, because the balloon image was slowly added onto, the image animation helps the user visualize how it transformed in each version.</span></p>","instructions":"<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Add image animation to show the progression across the balloon images!</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Under </span><strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\" style=\"background-color: rgb(204, 204, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">// project start</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">, create a new sprite with its image set to the first element of the </span><strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\" style=\"background-color: rgb(204, 204, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">balloonArray</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">. Position the sprite to appear </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">above</em><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> the 5 sprites created in the </span><strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\" style=\"background-color: rgb(204, 204, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">for</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> loop.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Animate the sprite’s image to rotate through each of the elements in the </span><strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\" style=\"background-color: rgb(204, 204, 204); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">balloonArray</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">. Update the frameInterval and loop parameters so that the images continuously cycle through.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Click ▶</span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><em> </em></strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">to see the development of the custom balloon image on screen!</span></p>","text":null,"type":null,"image":null,"videoUrl":null,"mediaType":null,"questions":null,"badges":null,"reflectionQuestions":null}],"title":"Pixel Art Dithering","project":{"editor":{"filters":[{"name":"controller","active":false,"blocks":[{"name":"game_control_sprite","active":true},{"name":"keyonevent","active":true},{"name":"keyispressed","active":true}]},{"name":"loops","active":false,"blocks":[{"name":"forever","active":true},{"name":"device_pause","active":true},{"name":"device_while","active":true},{"name":"pxt_controls_for","active":true},{"name":"pxt_controls_for_of","active":true},{"name":"pxt-on-start","active":true}]},{"name":"Math","active":false,"blocks":[{"name":"math_js_round","active":true},{"name":"device_random","active":true},{"name":"percentchance","active":true}]},{"name":"images","active":false,"blocks":[{"name":"Image_